    "_postman_id": "8d1e7c28-9f24-4ac6-8d43-3ab1d2a80d01",
    "name": "Discord DMs — Lab 3",
    "description": "# Discord DMs — Lab 3 Postman collection\n\nContains the original HTTP API examples plus read-only checks for Health and Service Discovery, including two-replica validation and recovery after a Discovery restart.\n\n**API URL:** Set `base_url` to a directly reachable instance (default `http://localhost:3000` for standalone development). The CPR Compose deployment does not publish Moderation HTTP ports, and the future two-replica Discord deployment should not publish a fixed `8086:3000` port. For end-to-end API requests use a Gateway URL only when that Gateway exposes the relevant endpoint and configure any required authentication.\n\n**Discovery URL:** `discovery_url` defaults to `http://localhost:18000`. Discovery is only reachable inside the CPR Docker network unless you publish/forward its port; do not expose it publicly.\n\n**Real data:** Set the IDs from a real created shift/session and its applicant/player before running the functional API workflow. An arbitrary UUID is not proof of an existing record.\n\n**Replica checks:** Run `Lab 3 - Service Discovery / 3. Verify Registered Replicas` only after deployment and health checks; `expected_replicas` defaults to 2. To test restart recovery, run `4. Capture IDs Before Discovery Restart`, restart only Discovery in Docker, allow the heartbeat interval (15s) and health monitor to complete, then run `5. Verify IDs After Discovery Restart`. The collection does not restart containers or attempt to re-register instances itself.\n\n**Important:** Discovery API checks verify service registration and health, *not* complete HTTP load balancing, gRPC circuit-breaking, or Socket.IO Redis cross-replica fan-out.\n\nThe pre-existing `Provision Session Channels` request documents an old mocked-Session flow; check whether that endpoint uses a real Session Service in the currently deployed version.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
